WEBVTT

NOTE week07-clip1-clip
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.992 line:2 align:center
In week six, contrastive learning
matched two views of the same ECG.

2
00:00:05.992 --> 00:00:11.940 line:2 align:center
CLIP keeps the same idea, but matches an
image with the text that describes it,

3
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.683 line:2 align:center
such as an H&E tile and its caption.

4
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:20.596 line:2 align:center
CLIP has two encoders. A vision
transformer encodes the image,

5
00:00:20.596 --> 00:00:26.309 line:2 align:center
and a text transformer encodes the
caption. Both produce 512 numbers,

6
00:00:26.309 --> 00:00:30.817 line:2 align:center
scaled to length 1, in
the same embedding space.

7
00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:36.275 line:2 align:center
Take a batch of four tiles and their
four captions. Comparing every tile

8
00:00:36.275 --> 00:00:41.865 line:2 align:center
with every caption gives a four by
four grid of cosine similarities.

9
00:00:41.865 --> 00:00:45.283 line:2 align:center
The true pairs sit on the diagonal.

10
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:52.544 line:2 align:center
Each row is divided by a temperature,
here 0.07, and passed through a softmax.

11
00:00:52.544 --> 00:00:59.550 line:2 align:center
The tumor tile then gives its own
caption a probability of 0.82.

12
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:04.214 line:2 align:center
The loss is cross-entropy in
both directions. Along each row,

13
00:01:04.214 --> 00:01:09.850 line:2 align:center
a tile must pick its caption. Down each
column, a caption must pick its tile.

14
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:14.417 line:2 align:center
The 2 are averaged, here to 0.18.

15
00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:21.480 line:2 align:center
CLIP was trained on 400 million image
and text pairs collected from the web,

16
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.530 line:2 align:center
in batches of 32,768 pairs.

17
00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:29.950 line:2 align:center
The temperature starts
at 0.07 and is learned.

18
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:34.418 line:2 align:center
BiomedCLIP uses the same
recipe on biomedical data:

19
00:01:34.418 --> 00:01:38.290 line:2 align:center
15 million figures and their captions,

20
00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:43.247 line:2 align:center
taken from 4.4 million
articles in PubMed Central.
